OpenPAM "Zingiber" (tag openpam-20250531), from https://git.des.dev/OpenPAM/OpenPAM,
committed as a plain tree (the tracked files of that tag, via git archive).

build.rs compiles lib/libpam into a static libpam.a with musl; nothing here is built with
autotools. OxideBSD's PAM modules are Rust (lib/libpam/modules), and link into each program.

Local changes (see LOGIN.md §6 in OxideBSD-doc):
- oxidebsd/config.h: the build configuration, in place of autoconf.
- include/security/openpam.h: with OPENPAM_OXIDEBSD, PAM_MODULE_ENTRY is empty (no linker sets).
- lib/libpam/openpam_static.c: looks modules up in a NULL-terminated table,
  openpam_static_modules[], that the modules library defines, instead of GNU linker sets.

To update: replace this tree with the new tag's git archive, then reapply the changes above.
